.TH BUMPPKG 1 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bumppkg \- pkgrel and version bump workflow with guards
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bumppkg status
.RI [ all | PKG ...]
.br
.B bumppkg history
.RI [ PKG ]
.br
.B bumppkg
.RB [ bump ] " " PKG ...
.br
.B bumppkg all
.br
.B bumppkg set all max
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bumppkg
bumps packaging revisions with deliberate friction. Never-published
packages are refused (bumping before first publish is churn; the
first publish claims the filename). A package bumped within the last
24 hours is refused (anti-loop; use
.IR --force ).
.B all
and
.B set all max
print the world-rebuild consequence (a full rebuild, easily days)
and require typing yes. Disabled recipes are never touched. Every
change lands in the release ledger shared with
.IR saphira-build " " rel-status .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show, do not write.
.TP
.B --force
Bypass anti-loop and never-published guards.
.TP
.B --yes
Non-interactive confirmation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $SAPHIRA_RELEASE_STATE/releases.jsonl
Append-only release ledger.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Bumped (or clean status/history output).
.TP
.B 1
Guard refusal, invalid name, or user declined.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
bumppkg status nginx
.br
bumppkg --dry-run nginx
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recipe (5),
.BR saphira (7),
.BR buildpkg (1),
.BR resolvepkg (1),
.BR saphira-build (8)
